{
  // pesc260805Only - forge the pesc260805 REBUILD bundle alone (no hubs, no bridges):
  // resolve -> forge -> standardBase -> materialize. This is THE LOAD (work order Phase 4.5):
  // the first time the rebuild's source + derived + synthetic + meta tiers have ever left
  // memory and been adjudicated by a real graph.
  //
  // WHY THIS IS NOT pescOnly WITH A NEW TOKEN. forges/pesc (the incumbent) and
  // forges/pesc260805 (the rebuild) carry DELIBERATELY DISTINCT standardName values
  // ('PESC' vs 'PESC260805', ruling D-6) so both can coexist in one graph while the rebuild
  // earns the incumbent's retirement on evidence. This recipe names ONLY the rebuild. The
  // incumbent's pescOnly.recipe.jsonc is untouched and still builds.
  //
  // WHY hubs [] AND bridges []. Phase 4.5's question is whether the NODES AND EDGES THIS
  // BUNDLE EMITS survive the bolt boundary intact - conservation, fusion, property fidelity,
  // referential integrity, traversability. A hub or a bridge would add nodes this bundle did
  // not emit, which is precisely the noise that makes a conservation-by-SET comparison
  // unreadable. The gates compare the forge's returned node/edge set against the graph; any
  // third party writing into the same graph would make a green indistinguishable from a
  // coincidence.
  //
  // NO roundTripStage - AND THE REASON CHANGED IN PHASE 5. THIS IS NOW THE STAGE-OFF SIBLING OF
  // pesc260805OnlyRoundTrip.recipe.jsonc, KEPT DELIBERATELY, not a recipe waiting for a validator.
  //
  // SUPERSEDED RATIONALE, PRESERVED BECAUSE NOTHING IS DELETED (work order standing rule 4). This
  // block read, from Phase 4.5 until 2026-08-07:
  //   "forges/pesc260805/parserDescriptor.ini DELIBERATELY does not declare a roundTripValidator
  //    yet - the validator is Phase 5's deliverable, and a declared-but-absent validator refuses
  //    the build by name on EVERY build (RT-13.3). Turning the stage on here would be asking for a
  //    verdict from an instrument that does not exist."
  // PHASE 5 FALSIFIED IT by declaring roundTripValidator=roundTripValidator.js. Left standing, the
  // text read as a CURRENT prohibition on turning the stage on, which is the opposite of the truth
  // and exactly the sort of stale rationale that outlives the condition it described.
  //
  // THE CURRENT REASON THIS RECIPE STAYS STAGE-OFF. It is the control half of an A/B pair. A
  // declared-but-never-invoked stage emits no error and fails no test, so the ONLY way to show the
  // opt-in does anything is to run both and compare: this recipe logs
  // "[roundTrip] stage OFF (recipe default (roundTripStage absent))" and writes a stage summary
  // carrying stageRan false, and -goldEvalCheck REFUSES its run directory BY NAME. Its sibling
  // runs the validator and passes that check. Deleting this recipe would destroy the control.
  //
  // GNC-001 is unchanged and still applies to both: DEV_pesc260805 is a SCRATCH graph and is NEVER
  // a golden. A DEV build is never renamed to GOLD_EVAL_ without a round-trip PASS, and creating
  // scratch graphs is never gated by that check.
  //
  // CONTAINER NAME. graphBuilder mints its product container as DEV_gb_materialize_<pid>_<seq>
  // (build.js:449). GNC-001 names this graph DEV_pesc260805, so the product is renamed with an
  // operational `docker rename` after the build - the same operational rename actions.js:1241
  // documents for DEV -> GOLD_EVAL promotion. The DEV_ prefix is preserved across the rename,
  // so replayManager's GNC-001 refusal guard still covers the container afterwards.
  //
  // VECTORIZATION IS OFF, DELIBERATELY, AND IT IS A DECISION NOT A DEFAULT. The build default
  // is --vectorize=true. Phase 4.5's five gates are conservation, fusion, property fidelity,
  // referential integrity and traversability; not one of them reads an embedding. DESIGN §7.2
  // query 2 ("find grade point average, get ONE hit not fourteen") is a test of the
  // SAME_DEFINITION cluster-representative rule - a DERIVED-tier property - and collapsing a
  // lexical hit list by cluster tests exactly that rule with no vector involved. Spending real
  // Voyage credit to embed ~42k never-before-embedded texts on a scratch graph, for gates that
  // cannot read the result, is spending for the appearance of completeness. Phase 5 does not
  // need it either (the round-trip emitter reads the source tier). Flip it on when a gate
  // actually asks a semantic question.
  "schemaVersion": "1.0.0",
  "recipeName": "pesc260805Only",
  "kind": "dev",
  "description": "Forge the pesc260805 rebuild bundle alone and materialize it - Phase 4.5 THE LOAD, the first real graph of the rebuilt PESC model.",
  "standards": [ { "token": "pesc260805", "version": "current" } ],
  "hubs": [],
  "bridges": []
}
